WEBVTT

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.510
Today we'll start practicing stunts.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.170
First, we'll put on a
demonstration for you.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.090
All you new recruits should watch closely!

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.010
The flyer is Haru, the spotter is Mizoguchi.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.760
The bases are Ichiro and...

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.090
I'll do it.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.710
Are you okay with this?

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.760
Let's go.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.590
1, 2, down, up, down, up!

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.460
Wow... I was all the way up
before I even knew it.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.420
Awesome!

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.010
He positioned the flyer in one go.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:02.710
This is what top-level technique looks like.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:04.710
You did it, Sho!

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.960
That hurts, Haru.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.670
Nice job!

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.050
That was really great!

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.630
So you got over your trauma!

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.050
Ichiro! Watch your big mouth!

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.510
Now we can have four stunt groups.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.800
But we're one flyer short...

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.050
Yahoo!

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.050
Amazin'!

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.510
You lifted him up so high!

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.510
There's our flyer!

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.420
Why's he doing that?

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.760
If you do cheerleading,
your Japanese will get super good!

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.590
And the girls will love it!

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.630
We'll treat you to some
fried pork curry with noodles.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.760
Dance like a squirrel, fly like a squirrel.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:44.010
Chen, do cheerleading with us.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.170
Please become our teammate!

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.840
Teammate?

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.380
That's right, you can be a Breaker, too!

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.880
Okay with me!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.460
Hooray!

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.460
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:26.510
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:32.260
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:36.340
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:42.170
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.460
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.670
<i>With that first step</i>

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.840
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.800
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.380
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.010
<i>just as you are</i>

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:02.170
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:08.710
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.340
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:15.210
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.460
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:23.590
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.010
Here are our routine's
formations for the qualifiers.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.130
With 16 people, we'll have four stunt groups.

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:50.710
The bases are Ichiro, Ton, Hisashi,
Takeru, Takuya, Takumi, Kin, and me.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:57.010
The spotters are Mizoguchi, Gen, Gin, and Doh.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.800
The flyers are Kazu, Haru, Saku, and Chen.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.510
There are several stunts
that I'd like us to try.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:12.550
One is the Single Base Extension.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.510
Another is the Half-Turn Elevator.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.170
Then there's the Three-Layer Pyramid.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.960
This adds a middle group
between the flyer and bases.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:34.760
Kin, Takeru, while you're both bases, I'd like
you two to be in the middle for the Pyramid.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.050
As a man, I cannot refuse your request.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:40.960
Yeah, we'll stand out right next to the flyer!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:46.460
We're aiming for uniquely masculine cheerleading
that's dynamic but doesn't rely on strength alone.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:49.050
If you polish your skills to perfection,
then you can surpass Dreams--

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.840
No, you'll surpass Sparks as well.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.800
Also, starting today, I'll be
recording the entire practice session

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.710
so that we can review
your performance later.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.800
Got that?

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.210
Right, let's get cracking!

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:05.010
All new members should
master the basics first.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.420
You'll start practicing these
stunts properly after that.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.710
Yeah!

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.550
B, B, Broccoli!

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:19.550
She'll really laugh at anything.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.380
Is he in elementary school?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.710
Takeru, this isn't the time
to be standing out!

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.710
The new guys are practicing tumbling.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.920
All recruits will do handstands.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.840
It's haaard!

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.550
Are you practicing handstands every day?

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.510
I'm not strong, so I can't do it.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:49.420
Handstands are tough.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:52.260
It's like you're saying you
could do everything else.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:56.880
Then, seeing you do it once
would be like finding a unicorn.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:03.420
Captain, I think Ando and Sakuma should undergo
intensive training and build up their muscles.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.550
Is this your training program for them?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.960
Push Ups x100

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.960
Sit Ups x100

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.960
Back Extensions x100

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.960
Squats x300

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:12.050
What?! I'm gonna turn into a body-builder!

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:16.050
You can't make progress until you can
do a handstand, so please do this.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.300
Well, once I get serious,
I'll do it no problem.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.760
You're using such a sophomoric excuse?
You'll end up a <i>neet </i>for sure.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:23.420
Me, a <i>neet</i>?!

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.800
We're in the middle of practice, guys.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.260
That's right. Knock it off, you two.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.550
That kind of language
is unacceptable, Hisashi.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.130
1, 2, down, up!

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.090
Go, fight, win!

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:43.760
Ah, that's right. I gotta get to work. Crap!

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.050
Huh?

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.300
Bro, I've got work, too.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.630
Huh? Don't tell me,
tell the captain and the coach!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.050
Thank you very much!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.050
We'll be leaving now!

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:01.880
Our team's not a corn cob. We can't
afford to drop off one by one.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.210
Captain, please tell them to schedule their
part-time jobs around our practice days.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:10.130
Everyone's got their reasons.
I can't force them to do that.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.090
You're early, Hisashi. Doing stretches?

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:26.420
Stretching's important for flyers,
but if they arrive later than a base like me,

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.800
then that means they have
zero self-awareness, don't they?

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.340
I've got a really bad feeling about this.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.710
And on the day we're practicing the Pyramid, too.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Coach Takagi

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Mizoguchi

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Kazu

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Tomorrow we're doing the Pyramid, so don't be late!
And on the day we're practicing the Pyramid, too.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Understood

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Thanks in advance

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.210
Yes

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.710
Kin's late?

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:42.340
We're terribly sorry.

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:49.380
His teacher wanted to meet
with him, so he'll be a bit late.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.630
My brother said he'll be late, too. He--

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.760
He slides, and he's safe!

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.380
Nope, you're out.

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.170
Sorry I'm late!

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.880
If a simple apology sufficed,
then we wouldn't need police.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.840
Have you never heard of
the phrase "Time is money"?

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.300
Then how 'bout this?

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.880
You pay 1,000 yen for
every minute you're late.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.920
So, Takeru, since you were
ten minutes late, you owe 10,000 yen.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.840
What is this, a clip joint?!

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.460
If it was, you'd owe 100,000.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:22.090
Doesn't sound like you're joking, Hisashi.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:25.420
Well then, starting tomorrow you
have to pay a fine. Sound good?

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:32.300
Every time Hisashi opens
his mouth, my heart stops.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.420
He always has to have the last word.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.920
The problem is that he's so serious.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Hisashi

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Good morning.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Hisashi

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Since I have time now,
I'm doing some solo training.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Hisashi

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Started Stretching.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Hisashi

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Muscle Training.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Hisashi

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
I'm going running now.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
Hisashi

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.160
I ran 10 kilometers.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:44.130
We have to do something about this.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.420
Hisashi!

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.710
Hisashi, come eat with us!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.380
Well, if you insist.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.510
Like a lady!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.460
You're even careful about what you eat.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.050
Obviously.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.510
In order to build up
your muscles effectively,

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:07.050
it's best to cut down on carbohydrates
and eat high-quality proteins.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:09.630
You're drinking protein, too?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.920
You all ordered an Extra-Large?

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.300
Ton, don't sway!

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.210
And don't look down!

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.550
I'm sorry.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.090
Ton, do you need a break?

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.880
Uh, yeah.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.050
I'm really sorry.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:39.550
S'all good. Take it easy.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.340
Hisashi, take his place.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.590
Right.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.340
Tono, you're giving up, aren't you?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.130
Okay, let's go.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.340
1, 2, down, up!

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.800
Yes! Just like that!

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:04.630
You're good, too, Hisashi.
Don't forget how this feels.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:06.090
Right!

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.630
Hisashi was full of energy, wasn't he?

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.170
He has a good feel for it,
so I think he'll make a great base.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.130
What's going on?

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:20.210
That's my line!

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:23.590
Just because work's almost over
doesn't mean you can loaf around.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.550
We're sorry.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:33.960
Kick things up a notch?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.510
Yes.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:40.170
There's only 2 months left until the qualifiers,
yet we still have members who can't do the stunts.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:44.010
If we're going to have a perfect routine,
we need to raise the level of the whole team,

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:47.010
or else we'll never score enough points.

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:50.590
Everybody's getting there
slowly but surely, don't you think?

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:53.710
And we have Coach Takagi
with us. Let's not rush things.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:58.090
You sound optimistic, but what
will happen if we don't qualify?

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.090
That's beyond irresponsible!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:06.050
Hisashi, I told you this before,
but not everyone can do what you can.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.510
And they don't have as much strength,
or as much time to spend on cheerleading.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:14.050
No! Nobody wants to
take cheerleading seriously.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.300
They all just goof around saying stupid things...

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.010
Isn't it the captain's job
to admonish them?

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:21.760
Get a grip already!

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.800
Hisashi...

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.050
I'm sorry. I didn't mean...

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:33.710
If we're going to enter a tournament,
then we need to work as hard as them.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:40.710
Is this Sparks' training regime? Wow.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:44.170
That's all I have to say. I'm going.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.760
Wait, Hisashi!

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:52.170
Hisashi...

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.500
Bandou Gym

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.840
My brother and I thought up a dance!

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:23.920
You may have us, but you simply have to
inject a little dance spirit into the routine.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.380
The dance scene will be perfect with this.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:28.670
These are for solo practice.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:30.130
Watch this and memorize it.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:32.960
I may be bad at it... but I will try.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.960
What a big help you two are.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:38.050
Well, we've caused you so much trouble...

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.380
Ando and the captain aren't here yet.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:45.340
Sorry I'm late!

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:50.630
It's rare for you not to be on time.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:53.460
I got delayed by blowing these things up.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.510
What's my fine?

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.210
Sparks has started
practicing with balance balls.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.420
Whoa, they have?

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.210
Yeah, Hisashi told me.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:13.590
There are other things I think we can do,
like squat stand-ups, that we should adopt.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.880
Good idea, keep 'em coming!

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:26.170
Ugh, I overslept.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.050
What else do you have to say?

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.170
Sorry I'm late.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.550
Your fine is 200,000 yen.

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:34.590
Take these and let me off the hook!

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:37.300
We're happy you
brought refreshments, but...

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:40.550
We're in the middle of practice now.
Let's eat them later.

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:43.590
There's no point if we don't
eat them while they're hot.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:47.550
Practice's only just started!
Let's take it slow!

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.510
Slow? Are you a turtle?

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:50.210
Huh?

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:52.510
No, that's an insult to turtles.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.010
You're below a turtle.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.010
Man, don't be so grumpy!

00:13:56.010 --> 00:14:00.630
You should eat up when you can eat,
and have fun when you have the time!

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.710
Right?

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:06.630
If you want to goof around, then be like
the grasshopper and live as you please.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:10.550
In return, don't drag down
the hard-working ants!

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:14.170
I said I'm sorry.
What're you so mad about?

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.090
If you have a problem,
then spit it out!

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:17.590
Well, then...

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:20.380
Do a handstand.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:26.210
You've stuck to the training program
I made for you and Sakuma, right?

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:29.130
I can do a handstand just fine!

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:33.800
Why would you say something like that,
Hisashi? Everyone's doing their best.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:40.590
Saku!

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.510
So you can do it without
leaning on a wall now!

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:46.510
Please don't be satisfied with so little.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:50.510
I'm trying... really hard.

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:52.460
Why the hell do you always
have to tear people down?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:55.590
It just proves you have no heart,
you rotten blockhead!

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:58.760
Look who's talking,
you rotten broccoli head!

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:00.260
You jerk!

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.920
--Hisashi!
--Takeru!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.340
Stop it, you two!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:07.920
Pork Buns

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.510
They finally came to blows.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.380
They sure did.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:19.420
Takeru is Takeru, but Hisashi is Hisashi.

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:21.380
They're like oil and water.

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:25.130
Isn't there any way for them to get along?

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.300
Why're you apologizing?

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:31.300
Because my winning streak ended.

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:32.920
All that matters is the next match.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:37.050
If you win that, you'll get
even stronger. I know you can do it.

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:40.420
Yeah. I'll definitely win my next one!

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:47.260
She just happened to feel out of it.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:52.090
Haruko will be fine.
She's always been strong.

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.460
Yeah...

00:15:56.420 --> 00:16:00.590
I'm sure she'll be all right...

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.110
Wataru Mizoguchi: I have
 something to discuss.
Tell our original members to
meet up at the caf tomorrow.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.420
A Christmas party?

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:09.210
Yes.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.300
An all male Christmas bash?

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:14.010
That's like fried octopus balls
without the octopus!

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:16.420
Ton, would your girlfriend
be okay with this?

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:20.260
So long as I'm free on
Christmas Eve, it's fine.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:26.090
I think it's a bad idea to leave things
as they are with those two... Especially Hisashi.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:29.010
Mizoguchi, you've been worrying about that?

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:30.920
He's a stoic guy, Hisashi.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.460
We just need to break
him outta his shell.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:36.170
We're the Breakers, after all.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.380
Right, let's do it together!

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:41.170
Okay, then let's plan our get-together.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:52.780
The calories...

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.870
Private Party

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:01.920
What a feast!

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:03.590
Wow, this is great!

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:06.090
Hooray for the Christmas bash!

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.130
This is a cake, right?

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:14.090
Do we have to eat it if we lose a bet?

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.340
That's some great taste, ain't it Bro?

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:19.090
Looks like their budget ran short.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:22.380
Huh? The women's cheerleading
team couldn't come today?

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:28.210
I also invited our coach, but she said she had
other business to attend to, and so wouldn't make it.

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:35.710
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:38.670
Where are these ladies you speak of?

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.760
Well, um...

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.840
Thank you all for coming here today.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.050
We really appreciate it!

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:47.090
Nice look, Haru!

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:49.130
Cool it with the pictures!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:51.670
I welcome all of them.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.920
Hey, we don't need to see your sexy side!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.630
Now for a few words from our captain.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:00.460
Let's forget about cheerleading
for today, eat and drink our fill,

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:02.130
and get to know each other better!

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:04.210
Everyone grab your glass!

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:07.800
Merry Breakers!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:14.710
Bro, can't I just have a taste?

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:17.760
Stop that, you'll break out in hives again.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.880
Takumi, you're allergic? That sucks.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.550
Hisashi, you can eat it, right? Have some.

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:27.550
No thanks, chili shrimp
has too many calories.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.510
Is that it?

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.960
You should be able to eat this.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.840
It's Bang-Bang Chicken.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.260
Thank you very much.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.590
Hisashi, your glass is empty.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.920
Oh, thank you.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:46.130
Next we'll hand out the presents!

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.880
Heads up!

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:51.960
I'm the first one!

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.090
All right, what've we got here?

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:59.090
Aw, hell no.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.780
<b>Caf Sunflower Meal Coupon Secret Menu</b>

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.510
Whoa, I love rice crackers!

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:12.630
Those are my family's.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.710
Wow, really?

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:19.760
I told them I was cutting back on carbohydrates,
but they insisted I bring them anyway...

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.210
I'm really sorry.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:27.800
Delish! How nice that I
get to eat some this tasty.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:29.210
Hisashi.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.550
What is it?

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:35.420
I went too far the other day.
I'm sorry about that.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:38.010
Me, too... I'm sorry.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:41.460
No, I'm the one who...

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:42.630
I'm sorry!

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:54.260
Why're these so dang good, Hisashee?

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:56.260
I'm Takumi, Gin.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:20:00.710
Dat sho? Bring me another beer, Hisashee.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:05.800
Hey, Hisashee, drink up!

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Coach Takagi

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Coach Takagi

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Coach Takagi

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Coach Takagi

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Tomorrow we'll
finish up the pyramid.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Check the video yourself

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Understood

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.640
Don't be late!

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:12.840
What? Chen, you were a
gymnastics athlete-in-training?

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:16.010
Yes. Thanks to that, I can do cheerleading.

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:18.420
It's so much fun to do it with everyone.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:19.960
This Christmas bash is the best!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.210
So he holds up his leg
when he gets excited.

00:20:25.130 --> 00:20:27.550
It's been harder than I thought.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:30.050
It certainly eats up a lot of time.

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:32.510
Kin, how many places
have you been to?

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.090
Same here.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:38.050
Everyone needs to take
a break now and again.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:39.050
That's true.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:40.510
Agreed!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:45.380
I want a break, too.
Let's take tomorrow off!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.210
Stop joking around!

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:55.630
You two are always taking time off, and yet
you still plan to miss practice tomorrow?

00:20:56.710 --> 00:21:00.300
This kind of crap is why we'll
never perfect the pyramid!

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:02.840
You inconvenience everyone
by taking time off.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:05.590
You're not little kids,
so why don't you get that?!

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:08.800
What the hell? You've got a big ego
for someone's who not even a captain!

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.960
I apologized, didn't I?

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.460
Man, what a waste of my time!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.630
--I get no satisfaction from your apologies, Broccoli Head!

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:16.170
--Both of you, calm down!
--I get no satisfaction from your apologies, Broccoli Head!

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.130
What was that, you bastard!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.510
Hisashee! How dare you
say that to my Big Bro!

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:23.340
Don't be so rude!

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:38.510
Hey, ma, these apples taste great...

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:44.010
I should've practiced by myself instead.

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:45.170
I'm leaving.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:46.710
Wait, Hisashi!

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:51.210
What do you want?

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:54.420
This is my Christmas present to you.

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:56.340
Let's all wear them together.

00:22:11.670 --> 00:22:15.260
This is the worst Christmas bash ever.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:18.960
By the way, what's a "bash"?

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:22.960
Strain

00:22:32.920 --> 00:22:36.460
<i>Without even thinking, I shouted a reply</i>

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:43.090
<i>The voice opening that new door</i>
<i>sounded like a tightly clenched fist</i>

00:22:43.090 --> 00:22:46.510
<i>Resounding with reassuring determination</i>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:49.880
<i>I think if I let out</i>
<i>(I've been waiting for this)</i>

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:53.170
<i>All my pent-up energy</i>
<i>(I can change something)</i>

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:59.760
<i>We've always been looking for</i>
<i>something this cool! Ain't that right?</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:02.670
<i>Feeling insecure</i>
<i>(Oh my God!)</i>

00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:05.960
<i>I fell into a funk</i>
<i>(Oh my pride!)</i>

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>Send that old me</i>
<i>(Don't give in!)</i>

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:09.710
<i>A solid cheer</i>
<i>(Go, go!)</i>

00:23:09.710 --> 00:23:14.210
<i>Make encouraging motions</i>
<i>(Let's dance together!)</i>

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:17.590
<i>Yes! Fly high, fly dive, up and away!</i>

00:23:17.590 --> 00:23:21.340
<i>Never hang your head and give up</i>
<i>(No!) </i>

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:24.670
<i>Break up, break out, break it to smithereens</i>
<i>(Yes!)</i>

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:27.960
<i>Smile together, break a sweat, show your guts!</i>
<i>(Guts!)</i>

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:34.590
<i>Strike a victory pose toward the blue sky</i>
<i>(Jump! Jump! High V!)</i>

00:23:34.590 --> 00:23:37.760
<i>Win over everybody's hearts!</i>

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:41.130
<i>Go for that moment when</i>
<i>you meet a sparkling smile</i>

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:49.260
<i>Go, fight! Go, fight, win!</i>

00:23:53.760 --> 00:23:56.050
Hisashi said he's going
to quit the Breakers.

00:23:56.050 --> 00:24:00.510
Well, with him gone, this awkward
atmosphere will clear right up, won't it?

00:24:00.510 --> 00:24:02.510
Is Hisashi leaving really okay?

00:24:02.510 --> 00:24:06.090
He had such high hopes
for the Breakers, and yet...

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:10.970
Next Episode: The Dawning of a Bond.

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:08.920
Next Episode: The Dawning of a Bond.

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:10.960
Let's go, Breakers!
